  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nRegardless of if [#commit-a-navigate-event](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#commit-a-navigate-event) being called when there are intercept handlers and different navigation types (the case calling [#resume-applying-the-traverse-history-step](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#resume-applying-the-traverse-history-step) in particular), it will continue by calling intercept handlers  and setting up the callback to wait for them.\n\nThis means that intercepting and regular navigations behave differently, since intercepted navigations will in the case of `\"push\"`/`\"replace\"`/`\"reload\"`_always_  resolve the committed promise before setting up calling intercept handlers. and the [#resume-applying-the-traverse-history-step](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#resume-applying-the-traverse-history-step) will at least be initiated before setting up calling intercept handlers. The problem with this is that the callbacks could run before the committed promise has resolved for non-intercepted and the intercepted `\"traverse\"` case. This is a problem for non-intercepted because even though there are not intercept handlers, `onnavigatesuccess` and `onnavigateerror` still fire.\n\nThe solution is to move the entirety of [step 9](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#commit-a-navigate-event:~:text=If%20endResultIsSameDocument%20is%20true) to the very end of [#update-the-navigation-api-entries-for-a-same-document-navigation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#update-the-navigation-api-entries-for-a-same-document-navigation).",
